## 6. PM Task Procedures

### 6.1 PM Work Order Process

| Step | Action | Responsibility | System |
|------|--------|----------------|--------|
| 1 | PM work order auto-generated based on schedule | CMMS | Automated |
| 2 | Work order assigned to technician | Maintenance Supervisor | CMMS |
| 3 | Technician reviews work order and gathers parts/tools | Maintenance Technician | CMMS / Crib |
| 4 | Technician coordinates with Production for equipment access | Maintenance Technician | Radio / Supervisor |
| 5 | Apply LOTO if required per PM task | Maintenance Technician | LOTO procedure |
| 6 | Perform PM tasks per checklist | Maintenance Technician | PM checklist |
| 7 | Document findings, readings, and completed tasks | Maintenance Technician | CMMS |
| 8 | Note any deficiencies or follow-up work required | Maintenance Technician | CMMS |
| 9 | Remove LOTO and return equipment to Production | Maintenance Technician | LOTO procedure |
| 10 | Close work order with labor hours and parts used | Maintenance Technician | CMMS |
| 11 | Review completed PMs for trends and issues | Maintenance Supervisor | Weekly review |

### 6.2 PM Execution Requirements

| Requirement | Standard |
|-------------|----------|
| PM Compliance Rate | ≥95% completed within scheduled window |
| PM Window | ±3 days for weekly; ±7 days for monthly; ±14 days for quarterly |
| LOTO Required | Per equipment-specific LOTO procedure |
| Documentation | All tasks documented; readings recorded; deficiencies noted |
| Parts Usage | Record all parts consumed; update inventory |
| Follow-up Work | Generate separate work order for repairs discovered during PM |

### 6.3 PM Deferral Procedure

PM deferral is permitted only under specific conditions:

| Step | Action | Responsibility |
|------|--------|----------------|
| 1 | Technician identifies inability to complete PM on schedule | Maintenance Technician |
| 2 | Technician notifies Maintenance Supervisor with reason | Maintenance Technician |
| 3 | Supervisor evaluates risk of deferral | Maintenance Supervisor |
| 4 | If Class A equipment, Plant Manager approval required | Plant Manager |
| 5 | Deferral approved and new date assigned (max 7 days for Class A/B) | Maintenance Supervisor |
| 6 | Deferral documented in CMMS with reason and approval | Maintenance Supervisor |
| 7 | Deferred PM tracked to completion | Maintenance Supervisor |

**Deferral Limits:**
- Class A: Maximum 7-day deferral; Plant Manager approval
- Class B: Maximum 14-day deferral; Maintenance Supervisor approval
- Class C/D: Maximum 30-day deferral; Maintenance Supervisor approval
- Safety-critical systems: No deferral permitted

