## 8. Predictive Maintenance (PdM)

### 8.1 PdM Technologies in Use

| Technology | Application | Equipment Covered |
|------------|-------------|-------------------|
| Vibration Analysis | Rotating equipment health | Presses, compressors, motors >10 HP |
| Infrared Thermography | Electrical connections, motor health | Main panels, MCC, large motors |
| Oil Analysis | Lubricant and wear condition | Hydraulic systems, gearboxes |
| Ultrasonic Testing | Bearing condition, compressed air leaks | All bearings, air system |
| Motor Current Analysis | Motor and drive train health | Robot servos, conveyor drives |

### 8.2 PdM Schedule

| Technology | Frequency | Contractor/Internal | Report Turnaround |
|------------|-----------|---------------------|-------------------|
| Vibration Analysis | Monthly (critical) / Quarterly (standard) | Internal | 48 hours |
| Infrared Thermography | Quarterly | Contractor | 5 business days |
| Oil Analysis | Quarterly | External lab | 7 business days |
| Ultrasonic Testing | Quarterly | Internal | 48 hours |
| Motor Current Analysis | Semi-annual | Contractor | 5 business days |

### 8.3 PdM Action Thresholds

| Severity | Vibration (mm/s) | Temperature Rise | Action Required |
|----------|------------------|------------------|-----------------|
| Normal | <2.8 | <10°C above baseline | Continue monitoring |
| Alert | 2.8 - 4.5 | 10-20°C above baseline | Increase monitoring; plan repair |
| Alarm | 4.5 - 7.1 | 20-40°C above baseline | Schedule repair within 30 days |
| Critical | >7.1 | >40°C above baseline | Immediate action; stop if safety risk |

