## 10. Lubrication Program

### 10.1 Lubrication Standards

| Lubricant Type | Application | Brand/Specification | Storage |
|----------------|-------------|---------------------|---------|
| Hydraulic Oil | Press hydraulics, lift tables | ISO VG 46 AW | Bulk tank, filtered |
| Way Oil | Machine ways, slides | ISO VG 68 | 5-gallon pail |
| Gear Oil | Gearboxes, reducers | ISO VG 220 EP | 5-gallon pail |
| Grease (General) | Bearings, bushings | NLGI 2, lithium complex | Cartridge |
| Grease (High-Temp) | Heated equipment | NLGI 2, synthetic | Cartridge |
| Food-Grade Lubricant | N/A at {{ plant_name }} | — | — |
| Pneumatic Oil | Air line lubricators | ISO VG 32 | 1-gallon container |

### 10.2 Lubrication Schedule

| Frequency | Tasks |
|-----------|-------|
| Daily | Check hydraulic levels; grease high-cycle points |
| Weekly | Grease conveyor bearings; check pneumatic lubricators |
| Monthly | Grease all motor bearings; check gearbox levels |
| Quarterly | Oil analysis sampling; filter replacement |
| Annual | Hydraulic oil change (or per analysis); gearbox oil change |

### 10.3 Lubrication Procedure

| Step | Action | Responsibility |
|------|--------|----------------|
| 1 | Identify lubrication points from equipment lubrication chart | Maintenance Technician |
| 2 | Verify correct lubricant type for each point | Maintenance Technician |
| 3 | Clean grease fitting before applying grease gun | Maintenance Technician |
| 4 | Apply lubricant per specified quantity | Maintenance Technician |
| 5 | Wipe excess lubricant to prevent contamination | Maintenance Technician |
| 6 | Document lubrication completed | Maintenance Technician |
| 7 | Report any blocked fittings or unusual conditions | Maintenance Technician |

