## 11. Spare Parts Management

### 11.1 Spare Parts Classification

| Category | Definition | Stocking Policy |
|----------|------------|-----------------|
| **Critical** | Single point of failure; long lead time; no alternative | Stock 1-2 units on-site |
| **Essential** | Significant impact; moderate lead time | Stock based on usage rate |
| **Standard** | Common wear parts; short lead time | Stock per min/max levels |
| **Non-Stock** | Low usage; readily available | Order as needed |

### 11.2 Critical Spares Inventory

| Equipment | Critical Spare | Quantity Stocked | Lead Time (if not stocked) |
|-----------|----------------|------------------|---------------------------|
| Stamping Press | Main motor | 1 | 12-16 weeks |
| Stamping Press | Hydraulic pump | 1 | 8-10 weeks |
| Robot Cell | Servo motor (each axis) | 1 per type | 6-8 weeks |
| Robot Cell | Controller board | 1 | 8-12 weeks |
| Conveyor | Drive motor | 2 | 4-6 weeks |
| Conveyor | Gearbox | 1 | 6-8 weeks |
| Air Compressor | Air end | 1 | 10-12 weeks |
| Air Compressor | Motor | 1 | 8-10 weeks |
| Palletizer | Gripper assembly | 1 | 4-6 weeks |
| Electrical | Main breakers | 1 each size | 4-8 weeks |

### 11.3 Parts Requisition Procedure

| Step | Action | Responsibility |
|------|--------|----------------|
| 1 | Identify part needed from equipment documentation or CMMS | Maintenance Technician |
| 2 | Check crib inventory for availability | Maintenance Technician |
| 3 | If available, issue part from crib; record usage | Maintenance Technician |
| 4 | If not available, submit parts request in CMMS | Maintenance Technician |
| 5 | Maintenance Supervisor reviews and approves | Maintenance Supervisor |
| 6 | Purchasing orders part from approved vendor | Purchasing |
| 7 | Part received, inspected, and stocked | Maintenance Crib |
| 8 | Technician notified of part availability | Maintenance Crib |

### 11.4 Min/Max Inventory Levels

- Minimum levels based on lead time + safety stock
- Maximum levels based on usage rate + storage constraints
- Inventory reviewed monthly; adjusted quarterly
- Slow-moving inventory reviewed annually for disposition

