## 14. Operator Autonomous Maintenance (AM)

### 14.1 Autonomous Maintenance Tasks

Operators perform basic care tasks to extend equipment life and identify issues early:

| Task | Frequency | Responsibility |
|------|-----------|----------------|
| Visual inspection for leaks, damage, abnormality | Daily | Operator |
| Clean equipment and work area | Daily | Operator |
| Check fluid levels (hydraulic, lubricant) | Daily | Operator |
| Listen/feel for unusual sounds or vibration | During operation | Operator |
| Check guard and interlock function | Start of shift | Operator |
| Report abnormalities to Supervisor | Immediately | Operator |
| Complete daily equipment checklist | Daily | Operator |

### 14.2 AM Checklist Requirements

- Daily checklist posted at each piece of equipment
- Operator completes checklist at start of shift
- Abnormalities circled and reported to Supervisor
- Completed checklists collected weekly by Supervisor
- Trends reviewed at weekly maintenance meeting

